From 3d24348117413bddd06387f9f3404c32ec215215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:26:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] coreclr: build with a MinGW toolchain (clang/lld,
 x86_64-w64-mingw32)

The Windows build of src/coreclr assumes MSVC; with MSYS2 CLANG64:
- CMakeLists: MASM sources through enable_language(ASM_MASM) with UASM
  (-win64, __MINGW32__ selects the Itanium names in the stubs); the clang
  spellings of the MSVC options (-fms-extensions for C++, -fno-rtti,
  -fwrapv, ...); USE_STL (clr_std would clash with libc++); inc/mingw on
  the include path and msvc_compat.h force-included; /Zl and /EHa only
  with MSVC.
- No DAC, mscordbi, createdump, single-file diagnostics (out-of-process
  debugging); the CLRDEBUGINFO resource and /DELAYLOAD only with MSVC.
- coreclr.dll links the mingw import libraries; resource-only DLLs are
  linked with the C++ driver; MSVC linker flags only with MSVC.
- corguids from the checked-in MIDL output (as on Unix): no midl.exe.
- mscorwks_ntdef.src: DATA in upper case (lld); mscorrc.rc: string IDs
  that are HRESULTs reduced to their low word (rc.exe truncates them, as
  LoadString does; llvm-rc rejects them).
- GC: no vxsort (its std::numeric_limits clashes with libc++), introsort
  as on the other platforms.
- coreclr links clrmingweha (minipal/Windows, the /EHa support).
